# .vercelignore — files kept in the Git repo but EXCLUDED from the Vercel
# deployment, so they are not publicly served (they return 404). On Vercel,
# robots.txt is NOT protection and the Netlify `_redirects` 404 rule is inert,
# so exclusion-from-deploy is the correct mechanism for private/internal paths.
# Verified 2026-07-14.

# ── Internal operational tools (customer-lead CRM + backend script source) ──
# CRM stores data in localStorage + a Google Sheet; the deployed file has no
# PII or hardcoded webhook, but it is a private staff tool and must not be public.
# Staff access it locally or via an authenticated host — not the production URL.
crm/

# ── review-helper.html + reviews.json ARE deployed (noindex, unlinked, not in
#    sitemap) so the owner can send customers the /review-helper/ link after a
#    trip to collect Google reviews. Kept out of search, reachable by direct link. ──

# ── Internal helper tools (not linked, noindex) ──
driver-communication-helper.html

# ── Driver PWA dev tool (icon generator) — never public; the PWA itself
#    (driver-app/index.html) stays reachable-but-noindex per owner decision. ──
driver-app/icons/generate-icons.html

# ── Internal strategy / working docs (were publicly downloadable at /docs/*) ──
docs/
cleanup_report.md
marketing-context.md

# ── Serverless function source (does NOT run on Vercel; was served as static text) ──
# No hardcoded secrets (all process.env) but exposes backend architecture.
netlify/

# ── Inert Netlify config (Vercel ignores these; no reason to serve them) ──
_redirects
netlify.toml

# ── Developer / CI / build config (were publicly downloadable) ──
.claude/
.claudeignore
.github/
.gitignore
.nojekyll
.env.example
README.md

# ── Already gitignored (belt-and-suspenders in case ever committed) ──
_seo/
_archive/
.agents/
claude-skills/

# ── Superseded legacy page (noindex; keep out of the public deploy) ──
taj-mahal-agra-fort.html
